{"reference":"2 Samuel 8","book":"2 Samuel","chapter":8,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Reading in Context","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Second Samuel begins with David’s accession and the consolidation of his kingdom, then moves through the ark and the dynasty promise before turning to royal abuse, family violence, rebellion, grief, and a closing appendix. Chapter 8 belongs within that opening movement of consolidation.","verse_refs":["2 Samuel 1","2 Samuel 10:1-19","2 Samuel 11:1-27","2 Samuel 12:1-31","2 Samuel 13:1-39","2 Samuel 14:1-33","2 Samuel 15:1-37","2 Samuel 16:1-23","2 Samuel 17:1-29","2 Samuel 18:1-33","2 Samuel 19:1-43","2 Samuel 20:1-26","2 Samuel 21:1-22","2 Samuel 22:1-51","2 Samuel 23:1-39","2 Samuel 24:1-25","2 Samuel 2:1-32","2 Samuel 3:1-39","2 Samuel 4:1-12","2 Samuel 5:1-25","2 Samuel 6:1-23","2 Samuel 7:1-29","2 Samuel 9:1-13"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_samuel_008_eea222f80315b85dc73d7860"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"},{"id":"block_2","text":"Archaeology supports the existence of a later Davidic dynasty, but it does not establish an uncontested picture of the size, administration, or chronology of David’s kingdom. The chapter’s portrait of conquest and rule should therefore not be treated as archaeologically settled in every detail.","verse_refs":["2 Samuel 5","2 Samuel 6:1-23","2 Samuel 7:1-29"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_samuel_008_e13f22a8c3ec30bbbe82c3ed"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}